  "worked_solution": "If $F=P\\,i+Q\\,j$ is a vector field on ${R}^{2}$ and the partial derivatives of the components of $F$ all exist, then the *scalar* curl of $F$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\u2202Q}{\u2202x}-\\frac{\u2202P}{\u2202y} & =\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202x}(\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(xy))-\\frac{\u2202}{\u2202y}({y}^{2}+{e}^{x}) \\\\  & =y\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(xy)-2y \\\\  & =y(\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(xy)-2).\\end{aligned}\n$$",
